<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Ultrainfo (converted from the organizer's official GPX download)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata>
    <name>Warbird 100 course</name>
    <desc>One large backcountry loop from the Leslie County RV Park south of Hyden, KY, almost entirely inside the Daniel Boone National Forest. Track points and elevations copy the organizer's official GPX download ("Warbird 100 Final", linked from trailsick.com/warbird-100; retrieved 2026-08-13). The loop GPS-measures 102.19 miles with a 23-foot closure against the aid table's 102.2-mile cumulative frame, which governs pass miles (the race info PDF bills 103 miles and its CalTopo profile says 102.29). Station waypoints use the aid table's published coordinates where given (Bowens Creek, Bear Creek, Peabody, Sugar Creek, and the start/finish, whose printed longitude -8342894 is missing its decimal point) and otherwise sit on the track at each station's table mile.</desc>
    <link href="https://www.trailsick.com/warbird-100"><text>Warbird 100 official page</text></link>
  </metadata>
